<p>Pinnacle Sales now distributes <a href="/brands/us-stone-group/">US Stone Group</a> luxury surfaces across the Western U.S. — and for dealers, slab yards, and fabricators, the headline is this: <strong>you can buy by the container at quarry-direct pricing.</strong> If you move enough stone to fill a container, you skip the middle markup and land premium quartzite, marble, and porcelain at the best number we can offer.</p>

<h2>Who container buying is for</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Slab yards</strong> stocking trending material their local market is asking for.</li>
  <li><strong>Fabricators</strong> who want to own their inventory on signature lines instead of chasing single slabs.</li>
  <li><strong>Kitchen &amp; bath dealers</strong> ready to carry surfaces alongside cabinetry and capture the whole project.</li>
</ul>
<p>Container quantities earn the deepest tier on the price list. Singles and bundles are available too — but the container is where the economics get serious.</p>

<h2>How it works</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Mix to fill the container.</strong> A container is typically built from one hero material plus a second line to round out the count — like the current pairing below.</li>
  <li><strong>Quarry-direct access.</strong> US Stone Group holds direct relationships with the owners of the Cristallo and Patagonia quartzite quarries, plus a 20-year global sourcing network.</li>
  <li><strong>Inspected before loading.</strong> Every slab is checked before it ships, and any significant cracks or damage are disclosed up front.</li>
  <li><strong>One point of contact.</strong> Pinnacle Sales handles your quote, slab photos, inventory verification, and the order from first look to delivery.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Current Container: Perla Venata + Cristallo</h2>
<p>Here's a container ready to move right now — an exceptionally clean Perla Venata run finished with a Cristallo to complete the count.</p>

<h3>Perla Venata Quartzite — 60 slabs</h3>
<p>A beautifully clean, soft-cream Perla Venata with gentle gold-and-grey movement — one of the most versatile, design-friendly quartzites on the market. It reads bright and calm in a kitchen and pairs with nearly any cabinet color. <strong>This Perla Venata can be finished polished, honed, or leathered at no additional cost</strong> — your choice, your market.</p>
